<p>French police arrested a man early Saturday after he allegedly tried to ignite an improvised explosive device outside a Bank of America building in Paris’s 8th arrondissement. Prosecutors then opened a terrorism-related investigation into the attempted attack. Initial reports said a second person fled the scene and remained at large.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ohM9BlFRC-yHxkHyrYB2SaW1xHZsbrTbpJuHqyOg_JtiTv9l3ZnESmxw7wHi64La5fj8-9IC76J6S-IxXpJtHYVmVct6p35JsZ7CFlZA9v7T0vCxkfBL30uLtwY8-x_7pCgCl86K4RAGoHAkxT9a7GO4kcZsXdSAlPVMzbB69owll0azpQ' alt='Police officials stand alongside police and private security vehicles outside the Bank of America building in the 8th arrondissement of Paris on March 28, 2026, following an apparent bomb attack attempt.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Identity check: After his arrest, the suspect said he was both a minor and a Senegalese citizen, but authorities were still working to verify his identity, according to a police source cited by Dawn.</li><li>Arrest sequence: Sources said police arrested the suspect just after he placed the device outside the bank.</li><li>Explosive load: An initial assessment found that the ignition component contained 650 grams of explosive powder, heightening concerns about the device’s destructive potential.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Bank of America: The bank said the office was closed when the incident happened, and no employees were injured. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/france-paris-police-foil-attack-bank-of-america/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>French security services: The investigation quickly moved beyond local police, with the Paris judicial police and the DGSI domestic intelligence agency joining in. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1986460/police-foil-bomb-attack-outside-us-bank-in-paris'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/paris-suspected-bomb-attack-outside-bank-of-america-foiled/a-76579750'>Paris: Suspected bomb attack o